; SuiteCatalog.inix -- the Homer Suite's shared commands (10 November 2026): each command's name, its suite key, and
; one sentence that is word for word the same in every app, but for the app's own words: {app} its name, {thing}
; what it works on (record, line, item), and the like, listed under [words <app>]. A command with words of its own in
; one app has them under [words <command>|<app>]; a key an app keeps instead of the suite's, for a reason given, is
; under [keys <app>]. check.py's suite commands check fails a release whose key file says otherwise. Change a shared
; command here, then in every app's key file, so the suite stays one.
; APPS (1.235.0, 15 November 2026): apps= names the apps that have a command, as their key files had it that day. The
; suite commands check fails an app whose key file leaves out a command the catalog gives it, which it never asked
; about before. Add an app here when it gains the command; take it out only with the command.

[words DbDo]
lean=the current column's values
thing=record
things=records
current=the open database
targets=the current record or the marked ones
folder=the open database's folder
whose=record
targets_files=the open database's file
paste_what=text

[words EdSharp]
thing=line
things=lines
current=the current file
targets=the selected text or the current line
folder=the current file's folder
whose=text
targets_files=the current file
paste_what=text at the cursor

[words FileDir]
lean=the items' names
thing=item
things=items
current=the current item
targets=the current item or the marked ones
folder=the current folder
whose=item
targets_files=the current item or the marked ones
paste_what=items into the current folder

[words HomerView]
thing=line
things=lines
current=the current page
targets=the selected text or the current line
folder=the page's folder
whose=text
targets_files=the current page
paste_what=text

[keys FileDir]
; Invert Marked's exception ended on 17 November 2026: DbDo moved Inspect Record to Alt+I, so both apps invert on Control+I.

[handled DbDo]
; As for EdSharp and FileDir (1.240.0): real, and handled outside the router, by DbDo's grid keyboard model of 31
; October 2026 (DbDo.cs, the grid's ProcessCmdKey and formKeyDown) or by Windows and the record form. Its first
; export, on 15 November, listed these 33 and nothing else unaccounted for.
Cell Down=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Cell Left=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Cell Right=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Cell Up=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Cell Value Down=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code (24 November 2026: Alt+DownArrow says the cell alone)
Cell Value Up=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code (24 November 2026: Alt+UpArrow says the cell alone)
Column Bottom=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Column Top=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Context Menu=Windows' own Shift+F10, which opens the grid's context menu
Cursor Column First=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Cursor Column Last=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Cursor Grid End=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Cursor Grid Start=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Cursor Row End=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Cursor Row Start=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
First Marked=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Last Marked=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Mark and Next=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Mark and Previous=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Mark to First=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Mark to Last=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Next Marked=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Null Value=the record form's own key code
Previous Marked=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Say Cell Coordinates=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Say Column=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Say Column Header=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Say Row=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Say Row Header=the grid's virtual cursor, in DbDo's grid key code
Unmark and Next=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Unmark and Previous=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Unmark to First=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
Unmark to Last=the grid's marking keys, in DbDo's grid key code
View Cycle=the window's view keys, in DbDo's key code
View Cycle Back=the window's view keys, in DbDo's key code
; TOGGLE MARK'S SPACE (22 November 2026): Control+Space is the menu's key, but Space is handled in the grid's own
; KeyDown, so a Space within a second of a typed letter can go on to the ListView's type-ahead and a Space on a button
; or check box is never taken. No export can show it, so the whole command is set aside here; DbDo's auditPatterns
; still checks both keys against DbDo.cs.
Toggle Mark=Space in DbDo's grid key code; Control+Space on the menu
; SEMICOLON AND SLASH (24 November 2026): the suite's Mark and Unmark keys, taken in DbDo's grid KeyDown under Space's
; type-ahead rule, so a semicolon or slash typed in a text box is never taken; set aside for the same reason as Toggle Mark.
Mark Record=SemiColon in DbDo's grid key code
Unmark Record=Slash in DbDo's grid key code

[handled EdSharp]
; HANDLED OUTSIDE THE KIT'S ROUTER (1.239.0, 15 November 2026). check's exported keys step compares the keys a program
; declares, through /exportkeys, with the keys its key file shows. These commands are real but are not declared to the
; router, so they are not in the export and are not differences. Each says where it is handled.
Insert All Users Path=the JAWS script, in a file name box of an Open or Save dialog; elsewhere it passes Control+Shift+I on
Insert Script Path=the JAWS script, in a file name box of an Open or Save dialog; elsewhere it passes Control+I on
Next Word=the editing box's own Control+RightArrow
Previous Word=the editing box's own Control+LeftArrow
Web Client Utilities=the JAWS script

[handled FileDir]
; As for EdSharp: real, and handled outside the router, by FileDir's own key code because what the key does depends on
; the item under the cursor or on the Recycle setting.
Come up Level=FileDir's key code (Comma), which returns to the folder you left
Drive Letter=FileDir's key code, Alt with a digit
Go to Item=FileDir's key code, by the kind of item under the cursor
Go to Parent Folder=FileDir's key code, by the Recycle setting
Go to Root Folder=FileDir's key code
Open Item=FileDir's key code, by the kind of item under the cursor
Open Parent Folder=FileDir's key code, by the Recycle setting
Open Root Folder=FileDir's key code
Parent Folder=FileDir's key code, by the Recycle setting

[keys DbDo]
; THE READING KEYS (25 November 2026, Jamal's request): Alt+B, Alt+J and Alt+K read, wide and from the first record,
; the records a bookmark, Jump or Keywords picks out, without moving focus or changing the filter, and Alt+Shift+J and
; Alt+Shift+K the marked ones among them. List Bookmarks keeps Alt+Shift+B, the only way to go to a bookmark. DbDo's
; Jump Again and Keywords Again are retired (F3 repeats either), so those two commands are FileDir's alone.
List Bookmarks=Alt+Shift+B

[keys HomerView]
; F11 is Microsoft Edge's full screen
Elevate Version=Control+F11
; Control+F12 opens Edge's developer tools
Copy Log=Alt+Shift+L

[command About]
apps=DbDo, EdSharp, FileDir
key=Alt+F1
description=Say {app}'s version and release date

[command Alternate Menu]
apps=DbDo, EdSharp, FileDir, HomerView
key=Alt+F10
description=Pick any command from one list, in menu, name or key order

[command Announcement]
apps=EdSharp, FileDir
key=
description=Open the announcement of this version

[command Append Clipboard]
apps=EdSharp, FileDir, HomerView
key=Control+Shift+'
description=Add the clipboard text to the end of a file you name

[command Chat with AI]
apps=EdSharp, FileDir
key=F12
description=Ask the AI model on this computer a question

[command Clear Bookmark]
apps=DbDo, EdSharp
key=Control+Shift+B
description=Remove {what}

[command Clear Clipboard]
apps=EdSharp, FileDir, HomerView
key=Alt+Shift+'
description=Empty the clipboard

[command Clear Filter]
apps=DbDo, FileDir
key=Control+Shift+F
description=Show {what}

; SMALL WORDS IN LOWER CASE (21 November 2026, key groups): but, from, in, on, to, with and without, as in Go to
; Folder and Read Lean from Current; EdSharp already said "but", which kept it out of this command.
[command Close All but Current Window]
apps=DbDo, EdSharp, FileDir
key=Control+Shift+F4
description=Close every window but the current one

[command Close Window]
apps=DbDo, EdSharp, FileDir
key=Control+F4
description=Close the current window

; THE MARKING AND SEARCH GROUPS OF THE TWO LIST APPS (21 November 2026, key groups): FileDir takes DbDo's names and
; keys for the ends of a marking run and the first and last marked; DbDo takes FileDir's single Start and its Again
; keys; FileDir gains Reverse Jump.
[command First Marked]
apps=DbDo, FileDir
key=Control+PageUp
description=Go to the first marked {thing}

[command Last Marked]
apps=DbDo, FileDir
key=Control+PageDown
description=Go to the last marked {thing}

[command Mark to First]
apps=DbDo, FileDir
key=Control+Shift+Home
description=Mark every {thing} from the first to the current one

[command Mark to Last]
apps=DbDo, FileDir
key=Control+Shift+End
description=Mark every {thing} from the current one to the last

[command Reverse Jump]
apps=DbDo, FileDir
key=Control+Shift+J
description=Go to the previous {thing} whose {where} holds the text

[command Start Mark or Unmark]
apps=DbDo, FileDir
key=F8
description=Start marking or unmarking a range at the current {thing}

[command Unmark to First]
apps=DbDo, FileDir
key=Alt+Control+Shift+Home
description=Unmark every {thing} from the first to the current one

[command Unmark to Last]
apps=DbDo, FileDir
key=Alt+Control+Shift+End
description=Unmark every {thing} from the current one to the last

; THE SCRIPT GROUP (21 November 2026, key groups): V for scripts, Alt+V to invoke and Alt+Shift+V to edit, in both apps
; that run scripts.
[command New Copy]
apps=DbDo, FileDir
key=Control+Shift+N
description=Add a new {thing} with the current {thing}'s {copied}

