[command Path to Clipboard]
; EDSHARP ALONE SINCE 22 NOVEMBER 2026: FileDir's Control+C puts the current or marked items' full paths on the clipboard
; as text as well as files, so its Path to Clipboard only repeated Copy and was retired into it (Jamal's ruling: no two
; commands copy the same paths). EdSharp keeps it, since its Control+C copies the text, not the file's path.
apps=EdSharp
key=Alt+Shift+P
description=Copy the full path of {current} to the clipboard

